# Upstream: giac 2.1.0 moyal.cc. A discrete distribution lives on the integers, but its pmf at a non-integer k was the formula's value: poisson(2,3/2) = exp(-2)*2^(3/2)/(3/2)! (0.288), geometric(1/2,3/2) = sqrt(1/2)/2, negbinomial(3,1/2,3/2) about 0.193, poisson(2,-1/2) 0.054; geometric_cdf(1/2,3/2) = 1-(1/2)^(3/2) and negbinomial_cdf(3,1/2,3/2) the incomplete beta at k+1 = 5/2, where the cdf is the one at floor(k); poisson_cdf(2,-1/2) undef; the two-bound forms of poisson_cdf and geometric_cdf took cdf(k1-1) at k1 = 3/2 as cdf(1/2), and negbinomial_cdf(n,p,k1,k2) was cdf(k2)-cdf(k1), which leaves k1 out (aide_cas: Proba(x<=X<=y)). geometric refused k <= 0 and geometric_cdf k < 0. binomial took only doubles and fractions for its argument order: an MPFR k of 3/2 at Digits 40 gave a number, and binomial(5,0.5,3/2) swapped its arguments without end. negbinomial_icdf read the double field of its probability unconverted: negbinomial_icdf(3,1/2,1/5) = 0 (right 1; with 0.2 it was 1). Now a pmf at a number k off the integers, or below the support, is an exact 0; a cdf there is the cdf at floor(k) (0 below the support), a lower bound off the integers is ceil(k1); binomial refuses a non-integer MPFR k; negbinomial_icdf converts its probability to a double. A symbolic k keeps the formula.
